cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "BALDUR: The Baldur tensoralgebraic scripting language"
abstract: >-
  Baldur (Basic Algebraic Language for Deriving Unified Tensor Representations)
  is a minimalist interpreter language that natively supports symbolic
  manipulation of algebraic and index-notated tensor expressions, backed by a
  C++ tensor algebra implementation. It was developed as part of a master's
  thesis at the Institute of Continuum Mechanics (IKM), Leibniz University
  Hannover.
